{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-authored, and not ours to invent. These are the 61 measures from the partner",
    "agency's own measures spreadsheet, in their wording, their order and their",
    "domain grouping, so a tag here means to them what it means here.",
    "",
    "export_data.py reads this and never writes it. The list is expected to change as the",
    "agency revises it, which is why it is a data file rather than a Python list: updating",
    "it is an edit here and a re-export, no code change.",
    "",
    "  name    the exact wording from their spreadsheet. Never reword one - the workbook's",
    "          Indicators cells are matched against these strings and the export stops on",
    "          anything it does not recognise.",
    "  domain  which of the seven domains they filed it under. Kept so the two columns",
    "          cannot drift apart.",
    "",
    "Filling the workbook's Indicators column: tag a source only where it explicitly names",
    "or computes the measure. Deciding whether something loosely counts as 'Community",
    "belonging' is a judgement, and a guess here puts wrong information in front of a",
    "government agency. Blank is the right answer for most rows. The agency offered to",
    "complete the tagging themselves, so gaps are expected and are not a failure."
  ],
